WEBVTT

00:22.022 --> 00:26.943
THE ROTTEN EGG HATCHES

00:27.026 --> 00:29.028
HERBIVORE DRAMA CLUB
CARNIVORE DRAMA CLUB

00:29.112 --> 00:32.073
Yesterday, we heard from
the Festival of the Meteor committee.

00:33.158 --> 00:34.159
Um...

00:34.868 --> 00:39.247
"Splitting the show into two halves,
one for carnivores and one for herbivores,

00:39.330 --> 00:45.086
clearly contradicts
this year's theme of 'Live Together.'"

00:46.296 --> 00:49.883
"Therefore, we cannot allow you
to participate this year."

00:50.925 --> 00:52.677
- What?
- Seriously?

00:52.761 --> 00:54.179
- That's awful.
- Ridiculous!

00:54.262 --> 00:58.641
So we're going to be the year
to break the drama club's tradition?

00:58.725 --> 01:01.644
Isn't there something we can do?

01:03.271 --> 01:05.690
Are you just going to accept that, Bill?

01:05.774 --> 01:09.277
How are you gonna look
Louis in the eye after this?

01:09.778 --> 01:11.529
- He's right.
- Stop.

01:11.613 --> 01:12.989
This isn't Bill's fault.

01:14.032 --> 01:17.077
- Well, yeah, but...
- What do we do?

01:17.160 --> 01:19.954
Excuse me. Can I say something?

01:25.335 --> 01:28.588
Maybe we made a mistake after all.

01:29.297 --> 01:30.298
What do you mean?

01:30.799 --> 01:32.509
We voted, didn't we?

01:32.592 --> 01:37.263
To either split into two groups
or cancel the club altogether.

01:38.014 --> 01:39.015
<i>Right.</i>

01:39.516 --> 01:40.558
<i>As a result,</i>

01:40.642 --> 01:43.728
<i>to preserve the message
of coexistence and mutual prosperity,</i>

01:43.812 --> 01:48.358
<i>we decided to carry on
as two separate groups.</i>

01:48.983 --> 01:52.445
That's why we set up this partition.

01:53.238 --> 01:59.035
But is there a wall dividing participants
at the Festival of the Meteor?

01:59.536 --> 02:02.247
Of course not.
There's no such thing in the adult world.

02:02.330 --> 02:07.043
Then why do we
have to be split up at school?

02:07.710 --> 02:11.548
Because the school doesn't
want to deal with the risks.

02:13.007 --> 02:16.928
We should understand those risks
more than anyone.

02:20.306 --> 02:24.936
Do you all remember
what happened to my arm?

02:28.106 --> 02:29.649
<i>When it happened,</i>

02:29.732 --> 02:32.777
<i>I considered quitting the club
and dropping out of school.</i>

02:33.444 --> 02:38.700
<i>Just looking at carnivores made me
freeze up. I could hardly breathe.</i>

02:40.952 --> 02:43.329
After they put my arm back on,

02:44.455 --> 02:48.459
<i>I just sat in the hospital bed
staring at it.</i>

02:49.711 --> 02:53.298
<i>Sunlight and wind came through the window,</i>

02:53.381 --> 02:57.051
<i>and little by little,
I started to be able to feel it.</i>

02:58.678 --> 03:02.348
<i>It made me want to touch something
as soon as I had the chance.</i>

03:03.474 --> 03:05.602
And the first thing I wanted to touch was...

03:07.729 --> 03:09.105
Tao.

03:10.648 --> 03:14.193
I didn't choose
to be born in this fragile body.

03:14.694 --> 03:16.821
The same goes for Tao.

03:19.282 --> 03:23.202
When I went to see him in the hospital,
and he asked me to touch him...

03:25.872 --> 03:26.915
it made me cry.

03:28.458 --> 03:33.129
<i>You were in so much pain,
but you still thought of how I felt.</i>

03:34.213 --> 03:38.092
You brought down
the wall between us, Kibi.

03:39.844 --> 03:43.306
That's because I know you, Tao.

03:43.973 --> 03:47.393
We've been together
in this club for so long.

03:54.651 --> 03:57.070
I think we did make a mistake.

03:57.153 --> 03:59.322
It was a mistake
to follow the school's orders.

03:59.405 --> 04:00.240
Hey...

04:00.323 --> 04:03.868
Putting up a wall between us.
Not seeing, not touching each other.

04:03.952 --> 04:07.372
Sure, it may be safer, but I...

04:07.455 --> 04:11.292
We've experienced
the carnivore-herbivore problem firsthand.

04:11.376 --> 04:13.920
We have something inside us
only we can express.

04:14.003 --> 04:16.339
Even if we do,

04:16.422 --> 04:19.509
the school won't let
carnivores and herbivores work together.

04:19.592 --> 04:21.261
We can do it!

04:21.344 --> 04:24.889
We've gotten through so much together.

04:24.973 --> 04:28.101
That's right. During last year's festival,

04:28.184 --> 04:32.188
we thought it'd be canceled
after Louis suddenly disappeared.

04:32.272 --> 04:34.524
But you pulled it together for us, Juno.

04:34.607 --> 04:37.318
That was because we all worked together.

04:37.402 --> 04:38.403
Exactly!

04:38.486 --> 04:42.031
That's it! We can do anything
when we work together.

04:42.573 --> 04:45.576
That's right. Different species
means different perspectives.

04:45.660 --> 04:50.164
We know what we have to gain
when we put our strengths together.

04:50.790 --> 04:53.042
Do you think we can pull it off?

04:54.294 --> 04:58.006
Actors, sound, lights, props.

04:58.089 --> 05:01.301
If we all do our parts
like we always have,

05:01.384 --> 05:04.887
I know we can come together
and put on a show, wall or no wall!

05:05.930 --> 05:10.101
That's right. If we do that,
maybe we can participate in the festival.

05:10.184 --> 05:11.352
Hey, Els.

05:11.978 --> 05:14.522
Let's try talking to the committee again.

05:14.605 --> 05:16.482
- And the school!
- We can't just--

05:16.566 --> 05:17.692
Hey, Bill!

05:17.775 --> 05:19.819
What happened to you, man?

05:20.611 --> 05:24.449
Don't you remember why
Louis chose you to be club leader?

05:24.532 --> 05:27.035
That's right. What do you want to do?

05:28.202 --> 05:31.205
Well, I...

05:32.790 --> 05:35.126
Yeah. You're right!

05:35.209 --> 05:37.211
Leave the negotiations to me!

05:38.463 --> 05:39.630
All right, Bill!

05:39.714 --> 05:41.799
All right! I'll go, too!

05:41.883 --> 05:44.385
Dad always said,
"There's no nut you can't crack."

05:44.469 --> 05:46.512
Like you've ever cracked a nut yourself.

05:46.596 --> 05:49.140
I'll change, too. Just you wait!

05:57.523 --> 06:00.193
JUNGLE THEATER

06:00.276 --> 06:01.736
CLOSED TODAY

06:04.405 --> 06:06.282
<i>Is this the place?</i>

06:23.424 --> 06:26.219
Have you ever seen a strip show before?

06:26.886 --> 06:27.970
No.

06:28.763 --> 06:32.016
It satisfies one's appetite
and sexual desires at the same time.

06:32.100 --> 06:34.727
Quite the convenient show for a carnivore.

06:34.811 --> 06:37.021
You brought me here to see this show?

06:37.105 --> 06:39.941
This place has a famous dancer.

06:42.485 --> 06:43.820
An okapi.

06:43.903 --> 06:46.572
There are herbivores
working in the Black Market?

06:47.156 --> 06:50.493
She'll be dancing
at Melon's masquerade party.

06:51.119 --> 06:55.248
You'll be acting as her chaperone, Haruo.

06:55.331 --> 06:57.583
Why'd you choose that name?

06:57.667 --> 07:00.461
Melon is a male
in his twenties or thirties.

07:01.087 --> 07:06.217
He's a mix, with the horns of a gazelle
but the face of a leopard.

07:06.300 --> 07:09.011
How will I find him
if he's wearing a mask?

07:09.512 --> 07:11.722
I'll locate him.

07:11.806 --> 07:14.058
You'll hold him down.

07:14.642 --> 07:18.312
Show me what Gohin has taught you.

07:18.896 --> 07:21.399
You know everything about me.

07:21.482 --> 07:23.443
Your record of devouring...

07:24.152 --> 07:26.779
I could wipe that, too.

07:27.864 --> 07:30.908
You want to marry
that rabbit Haru, don't you?

07:32.952 --> 07:34.704
I'll see you at the party, then.

07:35.246 --> 07:36.497
Aren't we going together?

07:43.921 --> 07:45.882
You'll be able to hear me with this.

07:48.301 --> 07:49.302
Damn it.

07:51.053 --> 07:52.472
So you're Haruo?

07:55.850 --> 07:56.893
Yes.

07:56.976 --> 07:59.729
You're more innocent-looking
than I expected.

08:01.022 --> 08:02.106
<i>Legoshi.</i>

08:02.190 --> 08:07.111
<i>You're supposed to be a rich, spoiled brat</i>

08:07.195 --> 08:09.655
<i>who's interested in shady adult parties.</i>

08:10.198 --> 08:13.075
<i>Put on a good act, drama club boy.</i>

08:13.159 --> 08:15.328
- I just did the lights--
<i>- Don't speak.</i>

08:17.121 --> 08:19.457
<i>Don't say anything
about the investigation.</i>

08:19.540 --> 08:21.292
<i>It'll put the girls in danger, too.</i>

08:21.918 --> 08:22.919
<i>Look in my seat.</i>

08:24.545 --> 08:26.672
<i>Put that on when you get to the party.</i>

08:27.465 --> 08:28.466
Let's go.

08:28.549 --> 08:29.550
Right.

08:30.635 --> 08:32.929
Wait up, babe!

08:44.357 --> 08:45.358
This is Luna.

08:46.234 --> 08:48.694
Nice to meet ya, lady.

08:48.778 --> 08:52.323
Act like a manager
and quiet down, would you?

08:52.406 --> 08:54.992
Hurry up and get in already.

09:01.082 --> 09:04.585
Haruo, we'll only be peeking in
on the party today, okay?

09:04.669 --> 09:06.212
I know that.

09:06.879 --> 09:09.924
- Will any famous people there?
- The guest list is private.

09:10.007 --> 09:12.385
This is a secret elites-only party.

09:12.468 --> 09:14.971
If you break the rules,
you'll be thrown out.

09:15.054 --> 09:16.180
It'll be fun, right?

09:16.264 --> 09:18.975
"Fun" isn't quite the right word.

09:19.058 --> 09:21.018
Just remember this.

09:21.602 --> 09:24.230
Don't drink the red juice.

09:24.313 --> 09:27.191
One sip and you'll be gone.

09:27.275 --> 09:28.609
Gone?

09:28.693 --> 09:31.320
It'll make you give in to your desires.

09:31.404 --> 09:34.991
You mean like wanting to eat raw meat?

09:35.074 --> 09:38.411
We're all way beyond that stage.

09:39.161 --> 09:42.248
It suppresses carnivores'
meat consumption urges,

09:42.331 --> 09:45.293
and makes herbivores let their guard down.

09:45.418 --> 09:48.045
It's fun for carnivores and herbivores
to be equals,

09:48.129 --> 09:50.715
not distinguishing one from the other.

09:51.340 --> 09:54.510
It's an escape from the rules
and constraints of modern society.

09:55.011 --> 09:57.096
True coexistence.

09:57.888 --> 10:03.060
Though there is a chance of being overcome
by urges worse than craving meat.

10:04.520 --> 10:07.315
Someone goes missing every time.

10:07.398 --> 10:08.983
Really?

10:09.483 --> 10:12.903
So is that juice like... a drug?

10:12.987 --> 10:16.157
Who knows? Just don't go near it.

10:17.033 --> 10:19.076
Put the mask on and keep quiet.

10:19.160 --> 10:19.994
Right.

10:34.550 --> 10:35.885
Good evening.

10:35.968 --> 10:37.094
Evening.

10:41.891 --> 10:45.394
<i>I can't see or hear anything in this.</i>

10:47.938 --> 10:49.315
Good evening.

10:50.941 --> 10:52.193
Hey, you.

10:53.361 --> 10:55.613
That's my new chaperone, Haruo.

10:56.238 --> 10:57.239
Really?

10:57.782 --> 10:59.241
Say the password.

11:02.662 --> 11:04.372
The hippo's skin is...?

11:04.914 --> 11:06.332
The hippo's skin?

11:07.667 --> 11:11.379
<i>No one told me anything about a password!</i>

11:15.299 --> 11:16.300
Cheers.

11:32.274 --> 11:34.527
<i>Melon is here somewhere.</i>

11:35.653 --> 11:37.154
<i>The horns of a gazelle.</i>

11:37.238 --> 11:39.990
<i>The slender body of an herbivore.</i>

11:40.074 --> 11:42.243
<i>The curved spine of a feline.</i>

11:43.119 --> 11:45.371
Hey, that tickles.

11:45.454 --> 11:47.832
- You know you like it.
- Don't tease me.

11:48.582 --> 11:49.583
You're cute.

11:50.292 --> 11:53.421
- I love the shape of your breasts.
- It's my turn now.

11:56.298 --> 11:59.009
<i>How am I going to find him in here?</i>

11:59.552 --> 12:00.970
<i>Legoshi, can you hear me?</i>

12:01.971 --> 12:03.264
Yes, I can hear you.

12:03.931 --> 12:06.684
Why didn't you tell me about the password?

12:07.476 --> 12:10.938
"A hippo's skin is sensitive."
I told you that.

12:11.021 --> 12:12.356
<i>No, you didn't!</i>

12:12.440 --> 12:13.357
Oh.

12:13.858 --> 12:16.026
Do you see Luna dancing over there?

12:17.736 --> 12:18.863
Yes.

12:19.530 --> 12:22.158
<i>There's a male with antlers behind her.</i>

12:24.201 --> 12:25.202
Got it.

12:25.703 --> 12:29.373
<i>Now look at the couple
holding each other by the stage.</i>

12:30.541 --> 12:31.375
I see them.

12:31.459 --> 12:35.379
<i>One more. Sitting at the end of the bar.</i>

12:36.630 --> 12:37.631
Right.

12:37.715 --> 12:40.384
<i>Melon is one of these three.</i>

12:41.469 --> 12:42.887
How do we tell which one?

12:42.970 --> 12:44.430
<i>Take off their masks.</i>

12:44.513 --> 12:45.764
I said, how can we tell--

12:45.848 --> 12:47.475
Hey, good-looking.

12:48.350 --> 12:50.769
Why don't we go play over there?

12:51.937 --> 12:53.147
C'mon.

12:54.482 --> 12:55.816
<i>Don't be shy.</i>

12:55.900 --> 12:57.568
Hey, Legoshi!

13:06.494 --> 13:10.247
The Beastar's office is even higher up
than the mayor's?

13:10.331 --> 13:11.332
What a joke.

13:11.874 --> 13:12.875
So?

13:13.667 --> 13:17.796
Lately there has been an increase
in devouring cases among young animals.

13:18.839 --> 13:21.800
And the suppressant
manufactured by Horns Pharmaceuticals

13:21.884 --> 13:23.511
doesn't seem to be working, does it?

13:24.637 --> 13:26.972
Despite all those government funds.

13:27.765 --> 13:29.308
Is that all you want?

13:30.351 --> 13:33.020
Have you heard of the Black Market?

13:33.729 --> 13:37.233
Adult carnivores are going there in secret

13:37.316 --> 13:39.610
to satisfy their cravings for meat.

13:40.361 --> 13:42.238
It's a repulsive place.

13:42.821 --> 13:44.907
They say the meat sold there

13:44.990 --> 13:47.910
comes from animals
killed in accidents or by illness.

13:49.161 --> 13:50.162
But you know...

13:52.248 --> 13:57.753
There were once children sold there too,
which they called "live bait."

13:58.712 --> 13:59.713
LIVE BAIT CATALOGUE

13:59.797 --> 14:02.591
We found some sales records.

14:03.092 --> 14:05.177
And the contents were truly surprising.

14:05.261 --> 14:09.932
It turns out it wasn't only carnivores
purchasing live meat.

14:11.141 --> 14:12.476
Look here.

14:13.811 --> 14:19.024
An herbivore deer bought this cute fawn
for quite a hefty sum.

14:20.150 --> 14:22.027
I wonder if they ate it?

14:25.197 --> 14:30.244
That was 15 years ago.
If he was alive now, he'd be 18.

14:31.495 --> 14:33.873
The same age as your Louis.

14:36.750 --> 14:41.380
Did you know that there's also
a fight club in the Black Market?

14:41.881 --> 14:44.633
One of its popular fighters,
a rabbit named Kyuu,

14:44.717 --> 14:47.595
also survived being sold as live bait.

14:48.429 --> 14:52.641
I wonder if she remembers that fawn.

14:55.102 --> 14:59.815
I plan on putting these notes
through the shredder once my term is up.

15:00.399 --> 15:02.318
It's just a relic of the past.

15:03.068 --> 15:04.445
What is it you want?

15:04.528 --> 15:05.738
To tell the truth,

15:05.821 --> 15:10.910
I've got a favor I can only ask
of the head of the Horns Conglomerate.

15:17.291 --> 15:18.292
Watch your hands.

15:26.592 --> 15:28.218
I said don't touch it.

15:28.302 --> 15:29.637
I was just looking.

15:29.720 --> 15:31.722
Don't make childish excuses.

15:32.431 --> 15:33.265
Yes, ma'am.

15:36.226 --> 15:38.562
<i>Herbivores really are beautiful--</i>

15:39.063 --> 15:40.773
Don't get too excited, kid.

15:40.856 --> 15:43.067
- Your mask is fogging up.
- No, it's not--

15:47.863 --> 15:50.074
<i>It's getting hard to breathe
in this thing.</i>

15:51.033 --> 15:55.037
<i>I can't see a thing. It keeps fogging up.</i>

15:57.414 --> 16:02.836
Carnivores can put on a mask with horns
and pretend to be one of us,

16:02.920 --> 16:06.423
but us herbivores can't take ours off.

16:06.507 --> 16:09.969
Kind of an unfair rule, don't you think?

16:11.971 --> 16:13.305
Don't sweat it, man!

16:13.973 --> 16:15.015
You're right.

16:21.063 --> 16:22.231
<i>This smell...</i>

16:24.191 --> 16:25.484
<i>That was him.</i>

16:34.159 --> 16:35.160
<i>That was Melon.</i>

16:45.879 --> 16:49.591
<i>He's so graceful and elegant.</i>

17:11.030 --> 17:12.865
Mr. Yahya, I found him.

17:13.741 --> 17:14.742
Where are you?

17:15.242 --> 17:17.995
<i>A booth in the ceiling.
There are stairs behind the bar.</i>

17:18.537 --> 17:21.707
Understood. Don't move until I get there.

17:21.790 --> 17:22.791
<i>Got it.</i>

17:27.880 --> 17:29.256
<i>Ladies and gentlemen.</i>

17:29.339 --> 17:34.511
<i>Tonight we're serving Melda,
100 times stronger than the usual stuff.</i>

17:34.595 --> 17:37.931
<i>Only one glass each,
but I hope you enjoy every last drop.</i>

17:40.768 --> 17:45.147
Has the wolf come to eat the gazelle?

17:46.023 --> 17:48.567
You're no ordinary gazelle.

17:49.693 --> 17:50.694
I could smell it.

17:51.278 --> 17:54.198
Excrement gives off
the smell of its contents.

17:55.157 --> 17:59.578
Your urine smelled like meat.
Impossible for an herbivore.

18:00.704 --> 18:03.499
There's no fooling a dog's nose.

18:03.999 --> 18:04.917
Move.

18:08.670 --> 18:11.006
So? What do you want?

18:11.673 --> 18:12.716
You're under arrest.

18:13.425 --> 18:15.302
- Not by me, but...
- Under arrest?

18:15.385 --> 18:17.638
For what, exactly?

18:19.181 --> 18:20.766
Suspicion of mass slaughter

18:20.849 --> 18:24.311
and organ trafficking of large herbivores,
I think?

18:25.521 --> 18:28.023
My friend will be here soon.

18:28.816 --> 18:30.359
You mean this friend?

18:31.193 --> 18:34.863
It looks like he might be a while.

18:34.947 --> 18:38.909
Maybe you can keep me company
until he gets here.

18:38.992 --> 18:42.538
- Aren't you going to run?
- I haven't done anything wrong.

18:43.539 --> 18:46.125
Besides, I want to talk to you.

18:46.208 --> 18:49.586
You're not a purebred wolf either,
are you?

18:52.297 --> 18:53.757
I knew it.

18:54.800 --> 18:57.427
I'll take my mask off too. It's only fair.

19:08.689 --> 19:13.068
<i>It's like my own child is about to hatch.</i>

19:15.821 --> 19:19.575
How did you know that about me?

19:20.284 --> 19:24.246
Your frame is way too large
for a regular wolf,

19:24.329 --> 19:28.208
and you weren't able to
hide your interest in me.

19:28.292 --> 19:31.378
- I...
- What are you mixed with?

19:31.461 --> 19:34.673
Not a feline. Maybe a kangaroo?

19:34.756 --> 19:37.301
- A Komodo dragon.
- Really?

19:38.343 --> 19:42.723
- Your parents were wild.
- Actually, he was my maternal grandfather.

19:43.765 --> 19:44.892
<i>Wait...</i>

19:45.684 --> 19:49.021
<i>Why am I saying all this to a stranger?</i>

19:50.272 --> 19:54.902
That must have been
terribly difficult for your mother.

19:55.819 --> 19:56.820
My mother...

19:57.863 --> 20:01.074
killed herself when I was 12.

20:01.742 --> 20:05.704
I see. So you've hurt, too. I get it.

20:06.830 --> 20:08.498
At this party,

20:08.582 --> 20:11.793
carnivores and herbivores can tear down
the wall between the species

20:11.877 --> 20:14.963
and be free of the prejudices they face.

20:15.047 --> 20:18.342
They drink the juice,
wear a mask, and have a good time.

20:19.551 --> 20:21.970
Sounds nice, doesn't it?

20:22.054 --> 20:25.390
As a mix, I have no real family nor peers.

20:25.474 --> 20:27.684
I'm an incomplete being
that doesn't belong anywhere.

20:27.768 --> 20:30.646
My mother was mixed,
but she wasn't incomplete.

20:30.729 --> 20:34.775
She killed herself
because she was incomplete.

20:36.526 --> 20:39.988
A mix is nothing but a freak of nature.

20:40.072 --> 20:42.449
What do you mean?

20:42.532 --> 20:44.201
Exactly what I said.

20:45.118 --> 20:49.998
This society celebrates carnivores
and herbivores getting along, right?

20:50.791 --> 20:55.712
And yet it treats the children
that result from that as freaks. Weird...

20:55.796 --> 20:57.965
I don't think they're freaks!

20:58.548 --> 21:01.385
I think they're beautiful.
I see nothing wrong with them!

21:02.552 --> 21:06.556
What a boring and cliché thing to say.

21:08.183 --> 21:12.104
Say something funnier.
Don't you know any good jokes?

21:12.187 --> 21:15.941
- I don't really know any jokes.
- In that case,

21:16.024 --> 21:17.734
I'll use your body instead.

21:19.152 --> 21:23.365
Listen up, old horse.
Or should I say, world-famous Beastar.

21:23.448 --> 21:26.410
<i>Sending in a kid to do your dirty work?</i>

21:27.619 --> 21:30.372
<i>Now that's one funny joke.</i>

21:31.748 --> 21:37.296
<i>Yahya, I've got a joke for you, too.</i>

21:40.966 --> 21:42.259
Legoshi!

21:48.974 --> 21:49.975
<i>What do you think?</i>

21:51.643 --> 21:53.312
<i>Was it funny?</i>

21:56.064 --> 21:57.566
Cheers!

23:36.915 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Thomas Grathwol
